{"signature": "{\"text\": \"Here is a GCSE-style question. An electric fan receives 300 joules of energy. It transfers 180 joules usefully to moving air and 90 joules to internal energy stores. Part A, worth two marks: calculate the energy transferred by sound, assuming these are all the outputs. Part B, worth two marks: explain why the energy supplied equals the total energy transferred. For Part A, 300 minus 180 minus 90 equals 30 joules. Award one mark for the subtraction and one for 30 joules. For Part B, energy is conserved, meaning it cannot be created or destroyed; therefore, when all transfers are accounted for, total energy input equals total energy output. Award one mark for conservation and one for linking it to the energy balance.\", \"voice\": \"en-NG-AbeoNeural\", \"rate\": \"-4%\", \"eleven\": true}", "duration": 57.103673, "words": [["Here", 0.0], ["is", 0.406], ["a", 0.627], ["GCSE-style", 0.766], ["question.", 2.589], ["An", 3.39], ["electric", 3.646], ["fan", 4.261], ["receives", 4.667], ["300", 5.283], ["joules", 5.956], ["of", 6.397], ["energy.", 6.641], ["It", 7.5], ["transfers", 7.697], ["180", 8.406], ["joules", 9.265], ["usefully", 9.752], ["to", 10.321], ["moving", 10.53], ["air", 11.018], ["and", 11.331], ["90", 11.622], ["joules", 12.063], ["to", 12.458], ["internal", 12.655], ["energy", 13.212], ["stores.", 13.665], ["Part", 14.489], ["A,", 14.896], ["worth", 15.232], ["two", 15.604], ["marks:", 15.882], ["calculate", 16.567], ["the", 17.206], ["energy", 17.334], ["transferred", 17.81], ["by", 18.518], ["sound,", 18.773], ["assuming", 19.273], ["these", 19.911], ["are", 20.248], ["all", 20.503], ["the", 20.736], ["outputs.", 20.887], ["Part", 22.024], ["B,", 22.384], ["worth", 22.988], ["two", 23.383], ["marks:", 23.65], ["explain", 24.451], ["why", 25.02], ["the", 25.252], ["energy", 25.391], ["supplied", 25.786], ["equals", 26.424], ["the", 26.912], ["total", 27.04], ["energy", 27.539], ["transferred.", 28.003], ["For", 29.037], ["Part